&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and technically strong &lt;strong&gt;Accounting Senior Manager &lt;/strong&gt;to lead our cryptocurrency accounting operations and support complex accounting matters across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, hands-on role that combines ownership of the crypto accounting function with broader technical accounting responsibilities, audit leadership, and internal controls development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is comfortable operating in a fast-paced, evolving environment, navigating complex accounting and regulatory requirements, and partnering cross-functionally with business leaders, Finance, Legal, Compliance, and external auditors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will play a critical role in ensuring the accuracy, integrity, and scalability of our accounting processes as the business grows and evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital Assets Accounting &amp;amp; Financial Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end accounting function for the company&#39;s crypto and tokenization-related activities, including month-end and quarter-end close processes, reconciliation review, journal entry reviews, and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and enhance accounting policies, procedures, and controls related to cryptocurrency transactions, digital assets, and associated business activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with crypto business leadership to understand new products, transaction flows, and business developments, ensuring appropriate accounting treatment and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee accounting for crypto-related transactions, including digital asset holdings, transfers, fees, settlements, and other relevant activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Finance, Legal, Compliance, and other stakeholders to support regulatory reporting requirements applicable to the crypto business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process improvements, automation, and scalable accounting solutions to support growth in crypto transaction volumes and business complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary accounting point of contact for crypto-related initiatives, providing proactive guidance on accounting implications and operational considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit Ownership &amp;amp; Regulatory Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage the external financial statement audit process for the crypto business, serving as the primary liaison with external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate audit planning, prepare supporting schedules and documentation, resolve accounting questions, and ensure timely completion of audit deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal stakeholders to address audit findings, strengthen accounting processes, and implement appropriate remediation measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory examinations, inquiries, and reporting requirements related to the crypto business, in coordination with Legal and Compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain audit-ready documentation and ensure accounting processes are supported by effective internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Accounting &amp;amp; Complex Transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key technical accounting resource across the broader organization, researching and evaluating complex or nonroutine transactions under US GAAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare technical accounting memoranda documenting accounting conclusions, relevant guidance, and financial statement implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance and business leaders to evaluate the accounting impact of new products, strategic initiatives, contracts, and unique business arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support accounting assessments for complex topics, which may include revenue recognition, equity transactions, investments, business combinations, digital assets, and other emerging accounting matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor evolving accounting standards and regulatory developments, assess their impact on the company, and support implementation of new requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with external advisors and auditors to resolve technical accounting matters and ensure consistent application of accounting policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10+ years of progressive accounting experience, including experience in public accounting and/or a complex corporate accounting environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of US GAAP, technical accounting research, and financial reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing month-end close processes, preparing financial statements, and coordinating external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cryptocurrency, digital assets, financial services, fintech, or similarly complex transaction environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently research, analyze, and document complex accounting matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, implementing, or improving accounting processes and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and work across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills and the ability to translate complex accounting topics into clear, actionable guidance for non-accounting stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working both strategically and hands-on in a dynamic, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA with a combination of Big Four or national public accounting firm experience and industry experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience with cryptocurrency accounting, including digital asset transactions, reconciliations, custody arrangements, and related reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting regulated financial services or crypto-related entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading financial statement audits and working directly with external auditors on complex accounting matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SOC 1 and/or SOC 2 readiness, internal control frameworks, and audit evidence requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing accounting automation, improving financial systems, or scaling accounting operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with senior leadership on new products, business initiatives, or complex commercial arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an AI Security Engineer to own the technical security controls for how Alpaca uses AI. The scope includes identity for AI agents and automations, security requirements for AI tools and integrations, guardrails, and security logging. You will also assist in developing AI-powered security tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will keep those controls consistent as AI adoption grows, and you will work with the teams building with AI so security is part of the design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Enterprise Security Architect and works closely with AI Enablement, Engineering, DevOps, GRC, and the wider Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Team is 100% distributed and remote.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The core responsibilities of the AI Security Engineer are focused on AI access controls, secure AI platforms, guardrails, visibility into AI usage, and AI-powered security tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Identity and Access Controls:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent Identity: Define how AI agents, bots, and automations authenticate, what they can access, and how their actions are attributed and audited.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool Access: Own security requirements for AI tool integrations, including least-privilege access and credential handling.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Assistant Controls: Define and enforce security settings for approved AI tools, including data handling and access policy.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Least Privilege: Limit each agent and integration to the access it needs, and review that access when the integration changes.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure AI Platform, Tooling, and Response:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Requirements: Define security requirements for internal AI applications, including identity, data handling, secrets, and review of new integrations.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guardrails: Design and implement guardrails for AI applications and agents.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Reviews: Review new AI applications and integrations for security risks, and give builders clear, practical requirements.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Tooling: Assist Security Operations in developing AI-powered tooling that supports detection, investigation, and response work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safe Use in Security: Apply the same identity, data handling, and logging requirements to security team AI tools as to the rest of the company.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Telemetry Requirements: Define the security logging AI systems must produce, and work with Security Operations on detection.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Approved Use: Maintain visibility into AI tool usage and confirm it follows approved configurations.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Support: Lead the AI-specific aspects of security incidents, such as agent misuse or data exposure through AI tools.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call: Participate in the Security Operations on-call rotation after onboarding and cross-training.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards: Turn AI security standards into technical controls.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRC Partnership: Partner with GRC on AI governance and provide technical evidence for control design.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about Alpaca’s mission and what we’re building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in security engineering, application security, or cloud security roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience securing LLM applications, AI agents, or AI developer tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of AI-specific risks, such as prompt injection, data leakage, excessive agency, and insecure tool use (for example, the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with identity and access controls for services and non-human identities, including OAuth, service accounts, and secrets management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in Python or another general-purpose language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD security checks and cloud-native deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security operations or incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, especially when explaining risk to non-security builders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working cross-functionally and making pragmatic security decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to participate in an on-call rotation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-assisted workflows for security operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building security telemetry for AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Might Be&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves):&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing financial, trading, or other highly regulated platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing enterprise AI coding tools and AI integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy-as-code and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI governance frameworks, such as the NIST AI Risk Management Framework or ISO 42001&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance security rigor with operational efficiency and business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the AML/Compliance Analyst, you’ll partner with the Chief Compliance Officer of Alpaca Crypto LLC to support and execute the anti-money laundering (AML) and compliance operations for our digital asset platform. This role is critical to mitigating risk, conducting transaction monitoring, and ensuring that Alpaca&#39;s crypto offerings operate securely and in full accordance with regulatory standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Compliance Department team is 100% distributed and remote. This role will report directly to the Chief Compliance Officer, Alpaca Crypto LLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform daily review and disposition of transaction monitoring alerts (fiat and crypto) to identify unusual or suspicious activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investigate &amp;amp; Report:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct deep-dive investigations into complex user accounts and blockchain transactions. Draft high-quality narratives and prepare/file Suspicious Activity Reports (SARs) with appropriate regulatory bodies (e.g., FinCEN).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blockchain Forensics:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize on-chain analytics tools (e.g., Chainalysis, TRM Labs, Elliptic) to trace cryptocurrency flows, identify high-risk wallet interactions, and assess illicit finance risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KYC / EDD:&lt;/strong&gt; Assist with escalated Know Your Customer (KYC) / Know Your Business (KYB) reviews, Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD), and OFAC sanctions screening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rule Tuning &amp;amp; Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with the CCO and compliance engineering to refine and tune transaction monitoring rules, ensuring false positives are minimized while capturing actual risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with customer support, engineering, and product teams to integrate compliance controls seamlessly into the Alpaca API ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Need (Qualifications):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 2–5 years of experience in AML, transaction monitoring, or financial crimes compliance within a cryptocurrency exchange, fintech, or traditional financial institution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crypto Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong understanding of blockchain technology, digital assets, and the specific AML risks associated with the crypto ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Grasp:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of BSA/AML regulations, OFAC sanctions, and FinCEN guidance regarding virtual currency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to analyze complex financial data, connect the dots across different platforms, and write clear, concise investigative narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with blockchain analytics tools and traditional fiat transaction monitoring vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High level of self-motivation and the ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced, 100% remote startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt; Relevant industry certifications (e.g., CAMS, CGSS, or crypto-specific certifications like CCAS/Chainalysis Reactor Certification) are a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Monthly Stipend: USD $150 per month via a Brex Card&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Alpaca is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace dedicated to pursuing and hiring a diverse workforce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca Japan is the Japanese subsidiary of Alpaca, a U.S.-based fintech group, and is registered as a Type I Financial Instruments Business Operator with the Kanto Regional Finance Bureau (Registration No. 3024). We provide securities trading infrastructure and operational services to financial institutions in Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our business and product offerings continue to expand, we are seeking a Securities Operations Specialist to oversee back-office operations, primarily for Japanese equity trading.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be responsible for a broad range of day-to-day brokerage operations, including settlement, cash movements, position and balance reconciliation, corporate actions, and customer account administration. You will also work closely with global teams and external stakeholders, to ensure accurate and stable operations and continuously improve operational processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who can proactively identify issues, take ownership, and collaborate effectively with relevant stakeholders in a fast-paced startup environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end back-office operations for Japanese equity trading, including post-trade processing, clearing and settlement, delivery of securities and funds, deposits and withdrawals, and position and cash reconciliation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage customer account opening and ongoing account administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the segregation of customer assets and prepare or review statutory books and records, customer statements, and regulatory reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage corporate actions, including dividends, stock splits, and shareholder benefits, as well as related tax and withholding operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with counterparties, clearing and settlement institutions, custodians, and other external stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle and escalate operational issues, exceptions, and trade discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and improve operational processes, procedures, and internal control frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate in English with global teams, including teams based in the United States&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications (required):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three years of hands-on experience in Japanese equity back-office operations at a securities firm, with practical knowledge of areas such as post-trade processing, clearing and settlement, cash and position management, securities accounting, customer accounts, segregation of customer assets, and corporate actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the Japanese securities market and its clearing and settlement framework, including the Japan Securities Depository Center (JASDEC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with, or knowledge of, statutory books and records and regulatory reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level proficiency in both Japanese and English. English proficiency must be sufficient for business communications by email and chat, reviewing documents, and participating in meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple responsibilities accurately, take initiative, and work effectively with relevant stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;strong&gt;preferred):&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JSDA Internal Control Manager qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Japan-specific account structures and tax regimes, including NISA and specified brokerage accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Middle and back-office experience with Japanese and foreign equities, particularly Japanese equities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching new services or establishing and improving operational frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a startup or other fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving operational efficiency, including through system changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform business responsibilities in both Japanese and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Conditions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-time employee&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office attendance is required for system access around 3 times a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;職種名:&lt;/strong&gt; 証券オペレーションスペシャリスト（日本株）&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;職務概要:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpaca Japanは、米国発のフィンテック企業Alpacaグループの日本法人であり、関東財務局長（金商）第3024号登録の第一種金融商品取引業者です。日本の金融機関向けに、証券取引に関するインフラおよびオペレーションサービスを提供しています。事業および取扱商品の拡大に伴い、日本株取引を中心とした証券バックオフィス業務を担うオペレーションスペシャリストを募集します。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;本ポジションでは、日本株の決済、入出金、残高照合、コーポレートアクション、顧客口座管理など、証券会社における日々のオペレーションを幅広く担当していただきます。また、米国を含むグローバルチームや社内外の関係者と連携し、正確かつ安定的な業務運営およびオペレーションプロセスの改善に取り組んでいただきます。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;変化の速いスタートアップ環境において、自ら課題を発見し、関係者と連携しながら主体的に業務を進められる方を求めています。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;主な業務内容:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本株取引に関するバックオフィス業務全般（約定後処理、清算・決済、証券・資金の受渡し、入出金および残高照合）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;口座開設・顧客管理業務&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;顧客資産の分別管理ならびに法定帳簿、顧客向け帳票および当局報告への対応&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;配当、株式分割、株主優待等のコーポレートアクションおよび税務・源泉徴収に関する業務&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;取引先、決済機関、カストディアンその他の外部関係者との連携&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;オペレーション上の問題や例外取引への対応およびエスカレーション&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;業務プロセス、手順書および内部管理体制の整備・改善&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;米国を含むグローバルチームとの英語によるコミュニケーション&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;応募資格:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;＜必須＞&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;証券会社における、3年以上の日本株取引に関するバックオフィス業務全般経験（約定後処理、清算・決済、入出金・残高管理、証券会計、顧客勘定および分別管理、コーポレートアクション）の実務経験・知識&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本の証券市場および証券保管振替機構を含む清算・決済制度に関する理解&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;法定帳簿および当局報告に関する実務経験または知識&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ビジネスレベルの日本語・英語力（英語は、メール・チャット、資料の読解、会議での業務上のコミュニケーションができること）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;複数の業務を正確に管理し、関係者と連携しながら主体的に対応できること&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;＜あると望ましい＞&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;内部管理責任者資格&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NISA・特定口座など、日本固有の口座・税制に関する知識&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本株式・外国株式、特に日本株式のミドル・バックオフィス業務経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;新規サービスの立ち上げやオペレーション体制の構築・改善に携わった経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;スタートアップまたは変化の速い環境での勤務経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;システム変更等、業務効率改善経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;言語:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本語および英語の両方で業務遂行が可能&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;勤務条件:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;正社員&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;リモート勤務可能だが、週に数回程度システム利用のための出社が必要&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Take Care of You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive Salary &amp;amp; Stock Options&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Health Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400; text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;New Hire Home-Office Setup: One-time USD $500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
