&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an IT Security Engineer to own the security standards and controls that protect Alpaca’s workforce identities, endpoints, and critical business systems. The scope includes identity and access management, single sign-on, privileged access, multi-factor authentication, endpoint security, secure network access, and email security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will maintain those standards, measure how the controls are working, and partner with IT, who run devices and day-to-day administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Enterprise Security Architect and works closely with IT, DevOps, Engineering, GRC, and the wider Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Team is 100% distributed and remote.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Things You Get To Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The core responsibilities of the IT Security Engineer are focused on identity security, endpoint security, email and domain protection, and measurable control enforcement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity and Access Security:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IAM and SSO Standards: Define and maintain security standards for SSO and conditional access across cloud, SaaS, and internal systems.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-Factor Authentication: Own multi-factor authentication standards, including phishing-resistant methods, and keep them enforced.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privileged Access: Maintain privileged-access standards, approval policies, and periodic access reviews with system owners.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joiner, Mover, Leaver: Partner with IT and People teams so access changes are timely, complete, and auditable.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoint, Email, and Domain Security:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EDR Policy: Own endpoint detection and response policy and tuning, with IT handling deployment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Device Posture: Maintain device-posture and secure network access requirements for access to business applications.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control Measurement: Measure identity and endpoint controls and follow up where they are not met.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection Partnership: Work with Security Operations on identity, endpoint, and email detections and response playbooks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Admin Access: Maintain security baselines for administrator access to critical SaaS platforms and vendor accounts.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Security Events: Assess the identity and account impact when a SaaS provider or vendor reports a security event.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Email Security: Own email authentication standards and email security configuration.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain Protection: Maintain security standards for company domains and for monitoring lookalike domains.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phishing Response: Triage reported phishing and coordinate takedowns.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Response and Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Support: Lead the identity, endpoint, and email aspects of security incidents, including account containment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Call: Participate in the Security Operations on-call rotation after onboarding and cross-training.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement: Give IT and employees clear guidance on security requirements, so controls are adopted without slowing the business.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
