&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to join a growing fintech company during a pivotal stage of growth.&amp;nbsp; As the Senior Accountant, you will play a key role in strengthening and scaling our accounting operations, financial reporting, and internal controls.&lt;br&gt;Our Accounting &amp;amp; Finance team is fully remote and distributed. This role reports directly to the Assistant Controller and partners cross-functionally to support the company&#39;s continued growth and regulatory compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and document journal entries in accordance with GAAP and company policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and help optimize the monthly, quarterly, and annual close processes, including journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, and process automation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare accurate and timely monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and enhancement of internal financial reporting and reporting distribution processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the annual financial statement audit by preparing supporting documentation and responding to auditor requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the parent company on tax documentation and information requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a multi-entity environment, being a key resource to adjacent teams within the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with weekly reserve computations and related reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, document, implement, and maintain accounting policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ad hoc financial analysis, reporting, and special projects as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
