&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://files.alpaca.markets/disclosures/AlpacaRecruitmentPrivacyPolicy.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a Senior Brokerage Operations Associate (Canada). An experienced individual contributor who has lived dealer, clearing, and custody reality and designs every process as if manual work is temporary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You turn CIRO-aligned operating requirements into scalable, automated, auditable workflows that Product and Engineering can build against. You partner closely with the ACCC President / UDP, Compliance, Product, Engineering, and global Ops. Someone who influences through expertise, crisp documentation, and decision logs, not through a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is measured by launch readiness, STP and control quality, registered-account / tax operability, and systems others can run and not by headcount or heroic spreadsheet ops.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll walk into:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won&#39;t be starting from zero. You&#39;ll be owning live problems:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Getting ready to open: figure out how we open and maintain accounts, process trades, and hold client cash and securities on day one. Build that for ACCC rather than copying a manual process from another firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with partner brokers: define how a partner firm and ACCC split the work on accounts, trades, and holding client assets, so it still works as volume grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;After the trade: settlement in Canada (through CDS), trades that fail to settle, and corporate actions such as dividends and splits. Automate the routine cases and keep a clear list of exceptions, instead of running the book in spreadsheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Registered accounts and tax: TFSA, RRSP, RESP, and similar accounts. Cover who can open them, contribution rules, what a security cost, tax withheld on dividends and other income, and the reports clients and partners need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The day after launch: written steps for daily work, checks that our records match the custodian and the market, contacts at vendors and custodians, and a plan if a system or vendor fails. Have these ready before real client volume shows up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building Canada: clear handoffs between product, engineering, and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Account lifecycle &amp;amp; client/introducing-broker servicing (onboarding handoffs, KYC/AML ops interfaces, maintenance, transfers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trade lifecycle (capture, affirmation, clearing, settlement, fails, breaks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Custody &amp;amp; asset servicing (segregation, security movements, corporate actions, cash)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Books &amp;amp; records, reconciliations, exception management, and operational controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Registered accounts &amp;amp; tax ops: TFSA, RRSP, RESP and related wrappers; tax lots / cost basis; withholding; local reporting partners need to stay compliant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-2 production ops: runbooks, escalations, vendor/custody interfaces, BCP/DR operational playbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate Canadian reality into runnable process&lt;/strong&gt; — CIRO-aligned dealer/clearing/custody expectations, introducing–carrying dynamics, custody controls, and operational risk into SOPs, RACI, controls, and exception paths Product and Engineering can build against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation-first by default&lt;/strong&gt; —&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;redesign high-volume / high-risk / high-friction work for straight-through processing, rules, exception queues, and measurable SLAs, instead of spreadsheet heroics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-first operating lens&lt;/strong&gt; — Prototype and productize AI-assisted ops (exception triage, recon investigation, SOP Q&amp;amp;A, control-testing support, runbook copilots) with human oversight where risk or regulation requires it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-live and beyond&lt;/strong&gt; — Readiness for ACCC launch and early production; continuous improvement after go-live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar without managing a team&lt;/strong&gt; — Coach partners through expertise, crisp documentation, and decision logs; leave systems others can run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;ll measure success:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch readiness gates met with documented controls, SOPs, RACI, and runbooks Product / Eng / Ops can execute against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STP, exception, and reconciliation aging targets defined and trending the right way post go-live&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Registered-account and tax workflows ready when partners launch, rather than added later&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specs and decision logs that remove re-discovery for Product and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems and playbooks others can run after you, so knowledge sticks in the org and not only in one person&#39;s head&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are (Must-haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of hands-on experience supporting Canadian brokerage operations, including experience within a CIRO-regulated dealer, carrying broker, custodian, clearing firm, or global operations team servicing the Canadian securities market.&amp;nbsp; Candidates may be based in Canada or India, provided they have demonstrated Canadian market expertise.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in the plumbing: clearing / settlement, custody, CDS / CDSX (or equivalent), fails, corp actions, tax, cash / securities ops, account servicing, introducing / carrying arrangements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated depth in at least two of: clearing / settlement; custody &amp;amp; asset servicing; books &amp;amp; records / reconciliations; registered accounts &amp;amp; tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory-literate (CIRO / provincial securities / CSA context). You design operable controls, and you are not the UDP or compliance sign-off owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder: you&#39;ve redesigned and shipped process + tooling changes that stuck, not only run BAU&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical with automation and AI (workflow automation, rules engines, RPA, or AI-assisted ops). You know where AI helps and where controls must stay deterministic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written communication: SOPs, RACI, decision logs, and requirements that cross-functional teams can ship against&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you might be (Nice-to-haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
